{
  "title": "The for Loop — Repeating a Fixed Number of Times",
  "subtitle": "Automating Repetitive Tasks with range()",
  "topic": "5.1 • THE FOR LOOP & RANGE()",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      5.1 • Iteration & Loops\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>for</hlt> Loop & range()\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Instead of copy-pasting code 100 times, a <hlt>for</hlt> loop tells Python to repeat an action automatically for a fixed count!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy: Running Laps\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      A Track Lap Counter\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      If a coach tells you <em>\"Run 4 laps around the track\"</em>, you start at lap 0, run lap 1, lap 2, and lap 3, then stop. The <hlt>range(4)</hlt> generator produces exactly 4 iterations: <code>0, 1, 2, 3</code>.\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">for</span> lap <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">in</span> <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">range</span>(<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">4</span>):<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Completed lap\"</span>, lap)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Output:<br/># Completed lap 0<br/># Completed lap 1<br/># Completed lap 2<br/># Completed lap 3</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      2. The 3 Flavors of range()\n    </span>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px;\">\n        <strong>range(stop):</strong> <code>range(3)</code> -> Generates <code>0, 1, 2</code> (starts at 0, stops before 3).\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px;\">\n        <strong>range(start, stop):</strong> <code>range(1, 6)</code> -> Generates <code>1, 2, 3, 4, 5</code> (starts at 1, stops before 6).\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px;\">\n        <strong>range(start, stop, step):</strong> <code>range(2, 11, 2)</code> -> Generates <code>2, 4, 6, 8, 10</code> (steps by 2).\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}